# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, the checked-out bytes depend on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting, and a
# file can appear modified purely because it was opened on a different platform. Pinning both ends
# means the same bytes everywhere and no line-ending diffs ever.
#
# LF rather than native CRLF on Windows because the repository already stores LF, so this is the
# choice that changes nothing on checkout. Visual Studio, VS Code and PowerShell all read LF
# without complaint; the only file that was CRLF on disk was the solution, which git was
# normalising on commit anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf

# C# hunk headers, so a diff names the method it is inside rather than just the line numbers.
*.cs text diff=csharp

# Binary: never convert line endings, never attempt a text diff.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.nupkg binary
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.snk  binary
